Description: Power panel: choose what happens when the lid is closed
 Adds a "When the Lid Is Closed" group to the Power Saving page with
 "On Battery Power" and "When Plugged In" rows (Do Nothing / Sleep /
 Hibernate / Shut Down), like Windows' power options. They set the
 gnome-settings-daemon keys lid-close-battery-action and
 lid-close-ac-action. Hidden on machines without a lid. Hibernate and
 Shut Down only appear when the system can do them unattended.
Author: SB4-Edge-Linux
Forwarded: not-needed
